@startuml
title The render ledger — the life of one entry: dispatch owes a page

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam StateBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

[*] --> Expected : UniversalNavigator dispatches;\nrecords the expectation in the ledger

state Expected #fdfdfd
state "Closed" as Closed #eef6f5
state "Timed out" as TimedOut #f9efef
state Responded #fdfdfd
state "Raised" as Raised #f6e0e0

Expected --> Closed : internal_callback arrives,\nour_signature verified
Expected --> TimedOut : completeness.render_timeout_seconds\nwins the race (render /\ncallback / external_call)
Expected --> Raised : a REQUIRED member dies\n(raise + instrumented)

Closed --> Responded : merged (serial, deterministic)
Closed --> Raised : page-merge conflict\n(raise + instrumented)
TimedOut --> Responded : the navigator answers\nwhether or not the page rendered

Responded --> [*]
Raised --> [*]

note right of Expected
  One entry per dispatched piece of work.
  The completion callback closes it, or the
  page's completeness.render_timeout_seconds
  closes it first — whichever wins the race.
end note

note right of TimedOut
  A governance timeout is fatal.
  A user-facing timeout explains, in
  layman's terms, what timed out and,
  where useful, asks the person to retry.
end note

note right of Raised
  Two conditions raise and are instrumented:
  a page-merge conflict, and a dead REQUIRED
  member. Both are governance exceptions,
  not user-facing prose.
end note

note bottom of Responded
  A page reconciles when every required_member
  closes OR render_timeout_seconds expires
  (per the registry page's completeness).
  The UniversalNavigator holds the ledger;
  a satellite's tools answer through the
  UniversalNavigatorProxy as callbacks.
end note
@enduml
